  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rP00\rP01\rP02\rP03\rP04\rP05\rP06\rP07\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "Unless otherwise specified in the application the materials to be used for the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted along with work of making good shall be carried out in materials to match those of the existing building.  \r \rReason: To ensure that the appearance of the development respects the appearance, existing materials and built and natural features of the surrounding area. \r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 6 people at any one time acting as a single household and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen / dining rooms shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the amenity of neighbours and the residential character of the surrounding area. \r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until the six long-stay cycle parking spaces have been provided in full accordance with the approved details shown on drawing No. P01. The cycle parking facilities shall thereafter be permanently retained and kept available for cycle parking for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until waste storage and recycling facilities to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site have been provided within the development, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities to be retained for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure that adequate waste and recycling storage facilities are provided to meet the needs of future occupiers, promote sustainable waste management practices, and support borough-wide recycling targets.\r"
  ]
}